<spell-notebook "icon theming">
	<header level="1">
		Icon
		<header>An icon is a glyph used to represent something else.</>
	</>
	<icon-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-icon-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a `<ui-icons>` group,
			`:root`), or on the box through `::part(icon)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each
			through a private alias, so nothing inside blocks them.

			- Size tokens (`--ui-icon-size-huge` ...) rescale a whole step; `circular` and `bordered` replace the width and
			  height (`--ui-icon-circular-size`, `--ui-icon-bordered-size`).
			- The glyph takes `currentColor`, so `color` on the icon or its parent works too.
			- Never set the `--_ui-*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			:root {
			  --ui-icon-distance: 0.5em;
			}
			.toolbar {
			  --ui-icon-size-large: 1.25;
			}
			```
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-icon" playground>
				<ui-icon name="house"></>
				<ui-icon name="users"></>
				<ui-icon name="cloud"></>
				<ui-icon name="puzzle-piece"></>
				<ui-icon name="heart"></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			A theme changes an icon's colour, not its glyph.  To change the glyphs themselves, add another icon
			pack (Usage tab).
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
